//////////////////////// CODE ////////////////////////////////

1. Return type is `boolean` but returning `-1` and `1` (integers)
2. `return res` at end is **unreachable code** — `res` is also out of scope there

---

**If you want to find position (index) of x — change return type to `int`:**

```java
// User function Template for Java
/*
class Node
{
    int data;
    Node next;
    Node(int data)
    {
        this.data = data;
        this.next = null;
    }
}
*/
class Solution {
    public static int searchLinkedList(Node head, int x) {  // ✅ int not boolean

        if (head == null)     return -1;                    // base case → x not found

        if (head.data == x)   return 1;                     // found → position 1

        int res = searchLinkedList(head.next, x);           // recurse on next node

        if (res == -1)        return -1;                    // x not found in rest
        else                  return res + 1;               // add 1 to position
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Dry Run:

Input: `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> null`, x = `3`

```
        call 1:   head = [1]   1 == 3? No  → recurse
        call 2:   head = [2]   2 == 3? No  → recurse
        call 3:   head = [3]   3 == 3? Yes → return 1
        call 2:   res = 1  → return 1+1 = 2
        call 1:   res = 2  → return 2+1 = 3
```

✅ x = `3` found at position `3`

-----------------------------------------------------------
Input: `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> null`, x = `5`

```
        call 1:   head = [1]   → recurse
        call 2:   head = [2]   → recurse
        call 3:   head = [3]   → recurse
        call 4:   head = null  → return -1
        call 3:   res = -1     → return -1
        call 2:   res = -1     → return -1
        call 1:   res = -1     → return -1
```

❌ x = `5` not found → returns `-1`

